    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d39">

                <pb facs="0219" n="87" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg87"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">
                    Leahy Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 39 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Truman
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d39-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-29">29th May 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Prime Minister to President Truman.
                    Personal and top secret. Number 58.</p>
                <p>Your 48.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d39-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>I have sent the following telegram to Premier Stalin: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <list>
                            <item>“1. Your message of May 27.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d39-f3"/> I shall
                                be very glad to meet you and President Truman in what is left of Berlin in the very near
                                future. I hope this might take place about the middle of
                                June.</item>
                            <item>2. Have repeated this telegram to President Truman who has informed me that
                                this point was raised in your talks with Mr. Hopkins. All good wishes. I am very
                                anxious to meet you soon.”<anchor n="4" xml:id="d39-f4"/>
                            </item>
                        </list>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Prime</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d39-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d39-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the United States Military Attaché, London, via Army channels.</p>
            </note>
